WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.200
MyCampusView Academy. Robotics 101, video 11: The line-following algorithm.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.450
An algorithm is a set of clear steps to solve a problem.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:16.150
Our robot needs one simple algorithm to follow the line.

4
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.920
Two sensors, each black or white, give only four cases.

5
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.619
Both white: the line is between them, go straight.

6
00:00:26.669 --> 00:00:31.413
Left sees black: the line is going left, turn left.

7
00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:34.138
Right sees black: turn right.

8
00:00:34.188 --> 00:00:38.650
Both black: a cross line or the finish, so stop.

9
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.281
Here is the same idea as a flowchart.

10
00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:49.926
Read the sensors, check the cases one by one, set the motors,

11
00:00:49.976 --> 00:00:52.650
and go back to the start.

12
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.117
In code, we use if, else if and else.

13
00:00:57.167 --> 00:01:01.297
Each block matches one row of the table.

14
00:01:01.347 --> 00:01:07.150
Turning left means slowing the left wheel to TURN_SPEED.

15
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:14.395
Here is the algorithm running in the simulator on an S-shaped track.

16
00:01:14.445 --> 00:01:20.650
Watch the decision panel switch between forward, left and right.

17
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:29.643
Now watch what happens if the left and right rules are swapped by mistake.

18
00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:35.201
The robot turns away from the line and gets lost.

19
00:01:35.251 --> 00:01:38.150
This is a very common bug.

20
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:45.000
Next: Uploading and testing on a real track.
